        "reason": "Codex reads this **before** AGENTS.md at global scope and takes only the first non-empty file at that level, so a home holding a non-empty one ignores the instruction file this provider installs. An empty override does not silence the floor -- Codex skips empty files -- which is worth knowing before concluding that a present override is the reason instructions are not applying. Deliberately not owned: an override exists so a person can escape a managed floor, and a provider that owned it could remove the escape with `remove`.",
